\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. O God, of good the unfathomed sea!
\par Who would not give his heart to Thee?
\par Who would not love Thee with his might?
\par O Jesu, Lover of Mankind,
\par Who would not his whole soul and mind,
\par With all his strength, to Thee unite?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Thou shin'st with everlasting rays;
\par Before the insufferable blaze
\par Angels with both wings veil their eyes:
\par Yet free as air Thy bounty streams
\par On all Thyworks; Thy mercy's beams
\par Diffusive as Thy sun's arise.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Astonished as Thy frowning brow, 
\par Earth, hell, and heaven's strong pillars bow;
\par Terrible majesty is Thine,
\par Who then can that vast love express
\par Which bows Thee down to me, who less
\par Than nothing am, till Thou art mine?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. High throned on heaven's eternal hill,
\par In number, weight, and measure still
\par Thou sweetly orderest all that is:
\par And yet Thou deign'st to come to me,
\par And guide my steps, that I, with Thee
\par Enthroned, may reign in endless bliss.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Fountain of good! All blessing flows
\par From Thee; no want Thy fullness knows:
\par What but Thyself canst Thou desire?
\par Yet, self-sufficient as Thou art,
\par Thou dost desire my worthless heart;
\par This, only this, dost Thou require.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Primeval Beauty! In Thy sight
\par The first- born, fairest sons of light
\par See all their brightest glories fade:
\par What then to me Thine eyes could turn-
\par In sin conceived, of woman born-
\par A worm, a leaf, a blast, a shade?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7
\par \cf0\ulnone\b0 7. Hell's armies tremble at Thy nod,
\par And trembling own the Almighty God,
\par Sovereign of earth, hell, air, and sky:
\par But who is this that comes from far,
\par Whose garments rolled in blood appear?
\par 'Tis God made Man, for man to die!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 8\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 8. O God, of good the unfathomed sea!
\par Who would not give his heart to Thee?
\par Who would not love Thee with his might?
\par O Jesu, Lover of Mankind,
\par Who would not his whole soul and mind,
\par With all his strength, to Thee unite?
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

